WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.710 --> 00:00:06.390
&gt;&gt; So, good afternoon, everyone.

00:00:06.391 --> 00:00:08.140
My name is Eshan Sadasivan,

00:00:08.141 --> 00:00:09.810
and I'm the founder and CEO of

00:00:09.811 --> 00:00:11.855
PROSOC Innovators
Private Limited.

00:00:11.856 --> 00:00:13.400
I have Mr. Shreeshan,

00:00:13.401 --> 00:00:17.270
who is our technical team member.

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:20.475
First of all, I
would like to thank

00:00:20.476 --> 00:00:23.070
both MSRA and Samhita for

00:00:23.071 --> 00:00:26.310
giving us this opportunity
to present over here.

00:00:26.311 --> 00:00:29.810
We're a for-profit
social enterprise.

00:00:29.811 --> 00:00:32.455
I'm clearly stating,
we're not NGO.

00:00:32.456 --> 00:00:34.700
We're a for-profit
social enterprise.

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:38.340
PROSOC stands for
Products for Society.

00:00:38.341 --> 00:00:41.150
We are a product
innovation company

00:00:41.151 --> 00:00:43.010
that is trying to design and

00:00:43.011 --> 00:00:44.930
develop innovative products to

00:00:44.931 --> 00:00:47.210
serve the people in
bottom of pyramid.

00:00:47.211 --> 00:00:50.485
So, our first product
is in education domain,

00:00:50.486 --> 00:00:54.050
where we have developed
a school bag that can become

00:00:54.051 --> 00:00:55.700
a study table for

00:00:55.701 --> 00:00:57.380
those underprivileged
students who sit on

00:00:57.381 --> 00:00:59.915
floor and study with
bad body posture.

00:00:59.916 --> 00:01:02.770
Our second product is
in livelihood domain,

00:01:02.771 --> 00:01:06.015
where it's a compact, low cost,

00:01:06.016 --> 00:01:08.930
paper carry bag making machine to

00:01:08.931 --> 00:01:11.595
mass produce paper carry bags

00:01:11.596 --> 00:01:15.140
as an alternative to
polythene carry bags.

00:01:15.141 --> 00:01:18.930
So, this compact machine,
this low-cost machine,

00:01:18.931 --> 00:01:20.180
is going to create

00:01:20.181 --> 00:01:23.240
numerous employment
opportunities to

00:01:23.241 --> 00:01:26.545
rural women as well as
physically challenged people.

00:01:26.546 --> 00:01:28.760
So, these are our two products.

00:01:28.761 --> 00:01:30.390
DESKIT, the school bag,

00:01:30.391 --> 00:01:31.715
is in education domain.

00:01:31.716 --> 00:01:35.030
The paper bag making machine
is in livelihood domain.

00:01:35.031 --> 00:01:39.935
But today, I am pitching
here for our third product,

00:01:39.936 --> 00:01:41.980
which is in agriculture domain.

00:01:41.981 --> 00:01:45.500
This product is being
headed by Mr. Shreeshan.

00:01:45.501 --> 00:01:48.639
So, in agriculture domain,

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:55.280
we are trying to build a machine
to segregate areca nut.

00:01:55.281 --> 00:02:00.060
Areca nut is this,
supari, what we call.

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:06.194
To tell a bit about PROSOC,

00:02:06.195 --> 00:02:08.610
we started our journey
from IIT Kanpur.

00:02:08.611 --> 00:02:10.490
We got the company incubated

00:02:10.491 --> 00:02:12.980
in IIT Kanpur SIDBI
Incubation Center.

00:02:12.981 --> 00:02:15.805
We started it in October 2015.

00:02:15.806 --> 00:02:18.215
So, next month, we'll be
turning three years old.

00:02:18.216 --> 00:02:21.000
For now, we have
one product in market,

00:02:21.001 --> 00:02:23.075
DESKIT, the school bag.

00:02:23.076 --> 00:02:27.495
Paper bag machine, we'll be
launching in January 2019,

00:02:27.496 --> 00:02:29.795
three months down the line.

00:02:29.796 --> 00:02:31.945
The areca nut machine,

00:02:31.946 --> 00:02:33.985
the R and D has started,

00:02:33.986 --> 00:02:36.240
and we are seeking
now support from MSRA

00:02:36.241 --> 00:02:38.350
and other eligible partners

00:02:38.351 --> 00:02:40.830
who can help us
develop this product.

00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:46.110
So, this is areca nut.

00:02:46.111 --> 00:02:48.245
So, it's a commercial
crop in India,

00:02:48.246 --> 00:02:50.270
and India is the
number one producer

00:02:50.271 --> 00:02:52.570
of areca nut in the world.

00:02:52.571 --> 00:02:57.375
India produces 49.5 percent
of world's areca nut.

00:02:57.376 --> 00:03:01.174
So, areca nut, from a tree,

00:03:01.175 --> 00:03:04.315
this is the kind of fruit we get.

00:03:04.316 --> 00:03:07.990
Once it's harvested, once
the processing is done,

00:03:07.991 --> 00:03:10.030
we get 12 types of areca nut,

00:03:10.031 --> 00:03:12.275
as the box is being circulated.

00:03:12.276 --> 00:03:14.385
So, there are 12 types
of areca nut,

00:03:14.386 --> 00:03:16.325
which are produced
from a single tree.

00:03:16.326 --> 00:03:19.170
Now, a farmer who is
growing areca nut,

00:03:19.171 --> 00:03:21.540
if he can segregate this into

00:03:21.541 --> 00:03:23.780
12 different types and
sell in the market,

00:03:23.781 --> 00:03:25.385
he can earn more money.

00:03:25.386 --> 00:03:27.880
Back in old days,
what used to happen,

00:03:27.881 --> 00:03:30.950
they used to have
manual segregation of

00:03:30.951 --> 00:03:34.505
these areca nut into
12 different types.

00:03:34.506 --> 00:03:38.005
But nowadays, there is
huge shortage of labor.

00:03:38.006 --> 00:03:40.550
They can't get people
to work for them.

00:03:40.551 --> 00:03:43.075
So, there is this problem,

00:03:43.076 --> 00:03:44.910
where if they can't segregate it,

00:03:44.911 --> 00:03:47.260
they can't sell at
better price in the market.

00:03:47.261 --> 00:03:49.110
So, they're incurring huge loss.

00:03:49.111 --> 00:03:55.190
So, that's why farmers
are not finding

00:03:55.191 --> 00:03:57.460
this particular
commercial crop as

00:03:57.461 --> 00:03:59.900
an attractive alternative for

00:03:59.901 --> 00:04:02.440
them to carry
their agriculture forward.

00:04:02.441 --> 00:04:05.690
So, here, we are trying
to eliminate the problem

00:04:05.691 --> 00:04:09.465
faced by farmers by

00:04:09.466 --> 00:04:10.975
designing and developing

00:04:10.976 --> 00:04:13.780
an image processing
based machine which can

00:04:13.781 --> 00:04:15.930
segregate 12 different
types of areca nut

00:04:15.931 --> 00:04:18.465
for them and make their job easy.

00:04:18.466 --> 00:04:21.215
Also, the accuracy of
the machine is more,

00:04:21.216 --> 00:04:24.910
and it eliminates
the shortage of labor.

00:04:24.911 --> 00:04:27.355
Now, I would like
to call Shreeshan,

00:04:27.356 --> 00:04:30.950
who would continue
the presentation.

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:38.315
&gt;&gt; Hello. Is it audible?

00:04:38.316 --> 00:04:38.705
&gt;&gt; Yes.

00:04:38.706 --> 00:04:42.475
&gt;&gt; Yeah. I will explain
the process of segregation.

00:04:42.476 --> 00:04:44.015
We have two cameras,

00:04:44.016 --> 00:04:46.395
one from the top view and
another from the bottom view.

00:04:46.396 --> 00:04:51.210
We need these two because
you can see in those type,

00:04:51.211 --> 00:04:53.210
there are actually
two surfaces which

00:04:53.211 --> 00:04:56.225
are having two different
characteristics.

00:04:56.226 --> 00:04:57.900
That's why we need two cameras.

00:04:57.901 --> 00:04:59.380
Once the image is captured,

00:04:59.381 --> 00:05:02.625
it's sent to image
pre-processing unit,

00:05:02.626 --> 00:05:06.590
where we remove the noise and
we change the aspect ratio,

00:05:06.591 --> 00:05:13.635
and we convert it to corresponding
[inaudible] part and segment it.

00:05:13.636 --> 00:05:20.505
Then, we feed into
a trained neural network model,

00:05:20.506 --> 00:05:22.320
which classifies the areca nut

00:05:22.321 --> 00:05:24.399
into corresponding surface.

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:27.305
Depending on the top view
and bottom view result,

00:05:27.306 --> 00:05:29.390
we will come into conclusion

00:05:29.391 --> 00:05:34.225
what type of
the areca nut is given.

00:05:34.226 --> 00:05:36.360
Depending on that, we give

00:05:36.361 --> 00:05:38.505
the control signal
to microcontrol,

00:05:38.506 --> 00:05:42.250
which will segregate
the areca nut into 12 bins.

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:52.500
The 12 types of
areca nut are varied

00:05:52.501 --> 00:05:58.230
from the changes in
their texture in both views,

00:05:58.231 --> 00:06:02.220
and they are segregated
depending on that.

00:06:02.600 --> 00:06:06.030
The texture, physique,

00:06:06.031 --> 00:06:09.000
and colors differ from

00:06:09.001 --> 00:06:12.130
one another so that
we can segregate.

00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:18.195
For collecting the data,

00:06:18.196 --> 00:06:20.210
we classified whole 12 types

00:06:20.211 --> 00:06:22.320
into five different surfaces.

00:06:22.321 --> 00:06:23.640
In five different surfaces,

00:06:23.641 --> 00:06:26.870
only depending on the size
and the surface texture,

00:06:26.871 --> 00:06:29.110
we will get 12 types.

00:06:29.111 --> 00:06:33.150
We collected 700 image
for each surface so

00:06:33.151 --> 00:06:36.590
that we got 3,500 images.

00:06:36.591 --> 00:06:41.285
Using image augmentation
technique for each type,

00:06:41.286 --> 00:06:42.965
we increase up to 2,000 images.

00:06:42.966 --> 00:06:45.140
That's why we got 10,000 images.

00:06:45.141 --> 00:06:46.810
Right now, we are using

00:06:46.811 --> 00:06:49.410
Inception V3 model
for retraining,

00:06:49.411 --> 00:06:52.305
in that we are getting
75 percent accuracy.

00:06:52.306 --> 00:06:54.430
What we need is,

00:06:54.431 --> 00:06:56.795
Inception V3 is trained for

00:06:56.796 --> 00:06:58.415
classifying different objects,

00:06:58.416 --> 00:07:02.860
like cycle, those defect
structure, object, and color.

00:07:02.861 --> 00:07:04.160
That's why we can't use

00:07:04.161 --> 00:07:08.290
Inception V3 anymore because
it gives less accuracy.

00:07:08.291 --> 00:07:10.890
That's why we need a some, yeah,

00:07:10.891 --> 00:07:14.855
which is trained on
segregation of similar objects

00:07:14.856 --> 00:07:18.700
such as face recognition,
iris recognition.

00:07:18.701 --> 00:07:20.195
Those can be retrained,

00:07:20.196 --> 00:07:24.585
so that it will
give more accuracy.

00:07:24.586 --> 00:07:28.605
We need inputs regarding

00:07:28.606 --> 00:07:33.860
changing the preprocessing stage.

00:07:33.861 --> 00:07:38.070
We are using only HSV segmentation
technique and some of

00:07:38.071 --> 00:07:41.425
the OpenCV techniques to get

00:07:41.426 --> 00:07:46.510
the areca nut crop to
the corresponding aspect ratio.

00:07:47.690 --> 00:07:53.175
&gt;&gt; When we started this project
we visited many farmers.

00:07:53.176 --> 00:07:55.485
We visited more than 70 farmers.

00:07:55.486 --> 00:07:57.250
Areca nut is a commercial crop,

00:07:57.251 --> 00:07:58.820
which is in India mainly grown in

00:07:58.821 --> 00:08:01.255
three states: Karnataka,
Kerala, and Assam.

00:08:01.256 --> 00:08:03.000
So, visited many farmers in

00:08:03.001 --> 00:08:05.650
Karnataka as well as
Sogo Heart in Assam.

00:08:05.651 --> 00:08:07.555
When we interacted with them,what

00:08:07.556 --> 00:08:09.580
we got to know from them was,

00:08:09.581 --> 00:08:10.975
to solve the problem of

00:08:10.976 --> 00:08:12.710
labor shortage
they're facing today,

00:08:12.711 --> 00:08:15.485
they are ready to pay
up to four lakh rupees,

00:08:15.486 --> 00:08:18.135
to buy if a machine was
existing like that.

00:08:18.136 --> 00:08:20.600
So, a customer is ready
to buy a machine,

00:08:20.601 --> 00:08:22.665
which costs up to
four lakh rupees.

00:08:22.666 --> 00:08:25.610
Because areca nut being
a commercial core crop,

00:08:25.611 --> 00:08:27.570
they have good returns
on this crop.

00:08:27.571 --> 00:08:30.830
So, they don't mind
investing this amount,

00:08:30.831 --> 00:08:34.730
which can help them through
the process they have to do.

00:08:34.731 --> 00:08:37.275
One more thing is, here we

00:08:37.276 --> 00:08:39.900
are not looking for
support from MSRA or

00:08:39.901 --> 00:08:45.090
support from Southern
California University.

00:08:45.091 --> 00:08:47.595
Just for building
one algorithm for

00:08:47.596 --> 00:08:50.290
one particular agricultural
product over here.

00:08:50.291 --> 00:08:53.285
We want a general algorithm,

00:08:53.286 --> 00:08:55.120
which can be finally

00:08:55.121 --> 00:08:58.460
customized or advanced
as per requirement,

00:08:58.461 --> 00:09:01.545
to suit to different
agricultural products

00:09:01.546 --> 00:09:03.685
across the world and support

00:09:03.686 --> 00:09:06.900
multiple products
or multiple farmers

00:09:06.901 --> 00:09:10.710
for different
agriculture products.

00:09:10.711 --> 00:09:15.075
Thus far, we are requesting
for an overall support,

00:09:15.076 --> 00:09:18.730
so that we can have
a strong technology in place,

00:09:18.731 --> 00:09:22.155
which can be implemented
as per the requirement.

00:09:22.156 --> 00:09:26.180
We have got our grant
of 10 lakh rupees for

00:09:26.181 --> 00:09:28.290
this particular project from

00:09:28.291 --> 00:09:30.845
needy press came of
government of India,

00:09:30.846 --> 00:09:34.095
for developing the mechanical
prototype of the machine.

00:09:34.096 --> 00:09:36.240
So, we have some budget in

00:09:36.241 --> 00:09:39.530
place to take care of
the mechanical prototyping,

00:09:39.531 --> 00:09:43.065
but on the technology
development when

00:09:43.066 --> 00:09:44.250
it comes to the coding and

00:09:44.251 --> 00:09:46.860
the algorithm part,
there we need support.

00:09:46.861 --> 00:09:50.010
One more thing is,
we recently happened

00:09:50.011 --> 00:09:53.480
to get in discussion with
the Design Alpha people.

00:09:53.481 --> 00:09:56.790
Design Alpha is a company
based South of Kochi.

00:09:56.791 --> 00:09:59.645
So, they support
different startups to come up

00:09:59.646 --> 00:10:03.230
with hardware prototypes
or hardware products.

00:10:03.231 --> 00:10:04.790
So, we are in
discussions with them

00:10:04.791 --> 00:10:06.380
on this particular product.

00:10:06.381 --> 00:10:09.335
So, their expertise of
more than 30 years is

00:10:09.336 --> 00:10:10.410
going to help us develop

00:10:10.411 --> 00:10:12.765
the mechanical part of
this particular product.

00:10:12.766 --> 00:10:14.945
So, we are looking for

00:10:14.946 --> 00:10:17.915
this image processing and
neural networks support,

00:10:17.916 --> 00:10:19.520
artificially region support,

00:10:19.521 --> 00:10:22.055
so that this product
can become a reality.

00:10:22.056 --> 00:10:24.790
&gt;&gt; I meant to ask,

00:10:24.900 --> 00:10:28.930
what types of people
typically process areca nuts?

00:10:28.931 --> 00:10:32.140
So, would it be
small household farmers

00:10:32.141 --> 00:10:34.170
or cooperatives of farmers or

00:10:34.171 --> 00:10:37.150
larger factories that have

00:10:37.151 --> 00:10:40.060
middlemen giving them
nuts from farmers.

00:10:40.061 --> 00:10:43.405
Can those processes typically
afford machines like that?

00:10:43.406 --> 00:10:46.105
&gt;&gt; There are cooperative
societies called Mondays,

00:10:46.106 --> 00:10:48.040
where the farmers
come their produce.

00:10:48.041 --> 00:10:50.665
&gt;&gt; Those of the markets know?

00:10:50.666 --> 00:10:52.715
&gt;&gt; Yeah. Mondays are the places

00:10:52.716 --> 00:10:55.200
where the overall
segregation happens.

00:10:55.201 --> 00:10:56.880
So, if this machine
will be ready,

00:10:56.881 --> 00:10:59.830
the ideal target customer
will be the Monday owner.

00:10:59.831 --> 00:11:02.260
Because this person
will be able to afford

00:11:02.261 --> 00:11:04.245
a better speed and

00:11:04.246 --> 00:11:05.900
better processing
capacity machine

00:11:05.901 --> 00:11:07.480
at a better price point.

00:11:07.481 --> 00:11:09.000
&gt;&gt; So, how many people work at

00:11:09.001 --> 00:11:10.780
these Mondays doing this work?

00:11:10.781 --> 00:11:12.605
&gt;&gt; Yeah, now event when

00:11:12.606 --> 00:11:14.360
things areca nut
processing season.

00:11:14.361 --> 00:11:15.420
There will be typically

00:11:15.421 --> 00:11:18.235
50-60 women and men

00:11:18.236 --> 00:11:19.980
laborers who will be
regularly employed.

00:11:19.981 --> 00:11:21.400
So, that duration will be

00:11:21.401 --> 00:11:23.770
for three to four
months in a year.

00:11:26.070 --> 00:11:29.115
&gt;&gt; All right, what is
the other question?

00:11:29.116 --> 00:11:31.580
&gt;&gt; One quick question.
You mentioned

00:11:31.581 --> 00:11:34.300
that you have the
restrictions of who can

00:11:34.301 --> 00:11:40.275
access like for Los Angeles
can be accessed?

00:11:40.276 --> 00:11:43.015
&gt;&gt; Yeah, the images we accessed
have taken the images.

00:11:43.016 --> 00:11:45.270
We can give the access to you,

00:11:45.710 --> 00:11:49.420
or as if required we can
also take more images.

00:11:49.421 --> 00:11:54.710
&gt;&gt; So, I have just a
meta comment which is

00:11:54.711 --> 00:11:57.940
that overall goal
that you have of

00:11:57.941 --> 00:12:01.215
classifying a crop is
very good, I think.

00:12:01.216 --> 00:12:04.240
But, taking the example of
areca nut specifically may

00:12:04.241 --> 00:12:07.275
not be a good example
of AI for social good.

00:12:07.276 --> 00:12:08.770
Because areca nut is

00:12:08.771 --> 00:12:10.510
the primary reason for

00:12:10.511 --> 00:12:13.035
very high incidence of
oral cancer in India.

00:12:13.036 --> 00:12:15.105
It is the primary reason.

00:12:15.106 --> 00:12:18.615
&gt;&gt; But, mixed with
tobacco, then it'll cause.

00:12:18.616 --> 00:12:20.750
&gt;&gt; No, no, no. So,
areca nut, I mean,

00:12:20.751 --> 00:12:23.940
I come from Northeast,

00:12:23.941 --> 00:12:25.210
very close to Assam.

00:12:25.211 --> 00:12:27.410
It's widespread addiction.

00:12:27.411 --> 00:12:30.910
So, it tobacco the incidence
increases by several fold,

00:12:30.911 --> 00:12:32.650
but even without tobacco,

00:12:32.651 --> 00:12:34.085
there is enough research
to show that

00:12:34.086 --> 00:12:37.265
areca nut actually causes.

00:12:37.266 --> 00:12:40.270
&gt;&gt; As a dentist, I can
give you some perspective,

00:12:40.271 --> 00:12:41.620
not a technology person.

00:12:41.621 --> 00:12:44.900
So, yes, areca nut
is one of the things

00:12:44.901 --> 00:12:47.105
which ignites or accelerate

00:12:47.106 --> 00:12:48.885
the carcinogenic, that's true.

00:12:48.886 --> 00:12:52.085
So, but that is persist
areca nut what you get in pan,

00:12:52.086 --> 00:12:54.045
cathar, supari, what you add.

00:12:54.046 --> 00:12:55.790
But, this is like
the wholesale one,

00:12:55.791 --> 00:12:57.340
with the shell intact and all.

00:12:57.341 --> 00:13:00.250
So, it has some medicinal uses
also and if you presses it

00:13:00.251 --> 00:13:03.430
down to that supari form,
removing the outer shell,

00:13:03.431 --> 00:13:05.670
then it is one of
the things which

00:13:05.671 --> 00:13:08.205
can lead to if you
constantly chew on you,

00:13:08.206 --> 00:13:09.920
it causes irritation
to the oral mucosa,

00:13:09.921 --> 00:13:11.470
and from there you can
get this blistered,

00:13:11.471 --> 00:13:12.835
and it can gradually go

00:13:12.836 --> 00:13:14.455
up to the carcinogen,
that's true.

00:13:14.456 --> 00:13:16.630
But, they're talking about
wholesale crops here,

00:13:16.631 --> 00:13:21.160
so that's something, which
